@startuml sequence-2oo3-voting
skinparam sequence {
    ArrowColor #01579B
    ActorBackgroundColor #E1F5FE
    ActorBorderColor #01579B
    ParticipantBackgroundColor #E1F5FE
    ParticipantBorderColor #01579B
}

participant "Site A" as siteA
participant "Site B" as siteB
participant "Site C" as siteC
participant "Voting Engine" as voter
participant "Output" as output

autonumber

siteA ->> siteA: process_signal()
note right of siteA: Analyze train position,\ncompute signal state

siteB ->> siteB: process_signal()
note right of siteB: Analyze train position,\ncompute signal state

siteC ->> siteC: process_signal()
note right of siteC: Analyze train position,\ncompute signal state\n(different data → RED)

siteA ->> voter: stage_output(GREEN)
siteB ->> voter: stage_output(GREEN)
siteC ->> voter: stage_output(RED)

note over voter
  All outputs staged locally
  Not yet committed
end note

voter ->> voter: checkpoint_barrier(200ms)
note right of voter: Wait for all sites to synchronize\nTimeout if any site slow/faulty

siteA -.-> voter: ack checkpoint
siteB -.-> voter: ack checkpoint
siteC -.-> voter: ack checkpoint

voter ->> voter: sync_outputs()
note right of voter: All sites exchange and verify\ndata consistency

voter ->> voter: voting_2oo3()
note right of voter: Count: GREEN=2, RED=1\nMajority (≥2) = GREEN\nVoting SUCCEEDS ✓

voter ->> voter: identify_minority()
note right of voter: Site C disagrees with majority\nMark as faulty\nTrigger health monitoring

voter ->> voter: commit_output(GREEN)
note right of voter: Atomic commit to decision\nAll nodes agree on result

voter ->> output: send_output(GREEN)
note right of output: Output transmitted\nto external system\nA and B agreed

output ->> output: execute(GREEN)
note right of output: Action taken\n(e.g., set signal to GREEN)

note over siteC
  Site C isolated
  Health counter incremented
  May trigger failover if multiple faults
end note

@enduml
